The source was generated from the repository reader manuscript. It uses a single-column preprint layout adapted from the Yale arXiv template's long-form structure, without Yale branding or logo. The custom palette uses dark navy (#0B1F3A), black body text, light gray-blue table headers, color-independent figure labels, and booktabs-style tables. Major-section float barriers keep displays with the relevant argument and before References. The approved Overleaf output is synchronized to the canonical preprint PDF. Inspect arXiv's compiled PDF before submission.

Template design reference: Ngoc Bui, The Yale arXiv Paper Template, CC BY-SA 4.0, https://www.overleaf.com/latex/templates/the-yale-arxiv-paper-template/wsmyhmnffgcs. This source uses an independent article implementation and carries no Yale affiliation or endorsement.

The repository and evidence archive are linked in the manuscript. This version is a preprint candidate and has not completed peer review.
